  <h2 class="no-num no-toc no-ref" id="sotd">Status of This Document</h2>

  <p><em>This section describes the status of this document at the time of its
  publication.</em></p>

  <p>This is a Living Standard maintained in the
  <a href="https://github.com/nosial/OFD-Specification">nosial/OFD-Specification</a>
  repository. It is updated continuously; the date at the top of the document
  identifies the current revision. It is not a W3C Recommendation and has not
  been endorsed by the W3C or by any other standards body.</p>

  <p>This revision defines version 1.1 of the OFD interface, which is backward
  compatible with version 1.0, as described in [[#versioning]]. It defines the
  architecture, identification, data model, protocol fundamentals, interface
  methods, telemetry, and security and privacy considerations of the Open
  Federated Database. It is aligned with FederationLib,
  the reference implementation of this specification.</p>

  <p>Feedback and comments on this specification are welcome and can be filed as
  <a href="https://github.com/nosial/OFD-Specification/issues">GitHub issues</a>.
  Proposed changes are submitted as pull requests against the <code>dev</code>
  branch.</p>
</div>

